 phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/README.rst    | 17 ++++++++---------
 ...k_Stream.sdp => VLC_Network_Stream_H264.sdp} |  0
 .../isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H265.sdp         |  4 ++++
 phytec-gstreamer-examples/isp/vpu/README.rst    | 17 ++++++++---------
 ...k_Stream.sdp => VLC_Network_Stream_H264.sdp} |  0
 .../isp/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H265.sdp         |  4 ++++
 6 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)
 rename phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/{VLC_Network_Stream.sdp => VLC_Network_Stream_H264.sdp} (100%)
 create mode 100644 phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H265.sdp
 rename phytec-gstreamer-examples/isp/vpu/{VLC_Network_Stream.sdp => VLC_Network_Stream_H264.sdp} (100%)
 create mode 100644 phytec-gstreamer-examples/isp/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H265.sdp

diff --git a/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/README.rst b/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/README.rst
index 66ebd8754b82..215c6c4067ea 100644
--- a/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/README.rst
+++ b/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/README.rst
@@ -4,17 +4,16 @@ Gstreamer VPU Encoding Examples
 Scripts
 -------
 
-  - save-h264-mkv-1280x720.sh
-    This example saves a HD video stream from the connected camera, H264
-    encoded in an MKV file.
+  - save-h26x-mkv-1280x720.sh
+    This example saves a HD video stream from the connected camera, H264 or
+    H265 encoded in an MKV file.
 
-  - capture-h264-network-stream-1280x720.sh
-    This example streams an HD video stream H264 encoded to the network, which
-    can be accessed e.g. with VLC on a connected host PC.
-    The provided VLC_Network_Stream.sdp can be used to access the provided
-    stream on the host PC.
+  - capture-h26x-network-stream-1280x720.sh
+    This example streams an HD video stream H264 or H265 encoded to the
+    network, which can be accessed e.g. with VLC on a connected host PC.
+    The provided sdp can be used to access the stream on the host PC.
     Make sure to set the correct IP address of your target board in
-    VLC_Network_Stream.sdp and the correct IP address of your host PC in the
+    the sdp file and the correct IP address of your host PC in the
     script.
 
     Note: To improve the delay on the received stream you can adjust the
diff --git a/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream.sdp b/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H264.sdp
similarity index 100%
rename from phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream.sdp
rename to phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H264.sdp
diff --git a/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H265.sdp b/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H265.sdp
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..1aa181d531d7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/phytec-gstreamer-examples/isi/vpu/VLC_Network_Stream_H265.sdp
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+v=0
+m=video 5200 RTP/AVP 96
+c=IN IP4 192.168.3.11
+a=rtpmap:96 H265/90000
